<title>HONG KONG: Prince of Wales to attend Hong Kong handover.</title>
<headline>Prince of Wales to attend Hong Kong handover.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Prince of Wales will represent the Queen at ceremonies marking the handover of the British colony of Hong Kong to China in June, according to a Buckingham Palace statement released in Hong Kong on Thursday.</p>
<p>He will stay on the Royal Yacht Britannia while in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>More than 150 years of British colonial rule ends at midnight on June 30, 1997 when Hong Kong reverts to China.</p>
</text>
